3.Which attribute was used to specify which inner borders (lines between cells) should be visible?
A)frame
B)border
C)rules  //answer
D)grid

✅ Correct Answer: C. rules

Easy English Explanation

The rules attribute was used in old HTML tables to control which inner borders (lines between cells) are shown.

Example:
<table border="1" rules="rows">
  ...
</table>

rules values:

rows → Show only row lines.
cols → Show only column lines.
all → Show all inner lines.
none → Show no inner lines.
Why the other options are wrong?
❌ A. frame → Controls the outer border of the table.
❌ B. border → Sets the border size, not which inner lines appear.
❌ D. grid → Not a valid HTML table attribute.
Easy Trick to Remember 🧠
rules = Rules for inside lines (inner borders).
frame = Frame around the outside.
One-Line Memory:

rules = Controls the inner borders between table cells.

✅ Answer: C. rules


