The char attribute in a table cell is used to:

Table Attributes • Level: Hard

A)Set font
B)Align text on a specific character (like a decimal)  //answer
C)Count characters
D)Hide text

✅ Correct Answer: B. Align text on a specific character (like a decimal)

Easy English Explanation

The char attribute (used in older HTML tables) was used to align text on a specific character, such as a decimal point (.).

This was useful for aligning numbers neatly.

Example:
<td align="char" char=".">12.50</td>
<td align="char" char=".">345.7</td>

Here, the numbers are aligned at the decimal point (.).

Why the other options are wrong?
❌ A. Set font → Fonts are controlled with CSS.
❌ C. Count characters → char does not count characters.
❌ D. Hide text → char does not hide text.
Easy Trick to Remember 🧠
char = Character
Align on a character (like . or :)
One-Line Memory:

char = Align table text on a specific character (usually a decimal point).

✅ Answer: B. Align text on a specific character (like a decimal).


